"G Fund.\\\"\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 10, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [157, 1923, 384, 1942], \"page_id\": 53}], \"content\": \"7 Includes money market mutua\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 11, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [155, 1940, 734, 1968], \"page_id\": 53}], \"content\": \"includes money market mutual funds, mutual funds, and closed-end investment companies.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 12, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [803, 1728, 1448, 1879], \"page_id\": 53}], \"content\": \"a Source: Federal Reserve Board Treasury International Capital Survey. Includes nonmarketable foreign series, Treasury securities, and Treasury deposit funds. Excludes Treasury securities held under repurchase agreements in custody accounts at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York. Estimates reflect the 1989 benchmark to 1994, the 1994 benchmark to September 2001, the March 2000 benchmark to September 2002, the June 2002 benchmark to December 2003, and the June 2003 benchmark to March 2004.\\nb Includes individuals, Government-sponsored enterprises, brokers and dealers, bank personal trusts and estates, corporate and non-corporate businesses, and other investors.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 13, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [140, 94, 184, 130], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"52\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [539, 212, 1095, 248], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"INTRODUCTION: Market Yields\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"section_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [135, 266, 798, 361], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"The table in this section presents yields on Treasury marketable securities for maturities ranging from 1 month to 20 years.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [137, 370, 805, 804], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"Table MY-1 lists Treasury market bid yields at constant maturities for bills, notes, and bonds. These \\\"constant maturity rates (CMTs)\\\" are interpolated from the Treasury yield curve and published daily at Treasury's web site, www.ustreas.gov/offices/domestic-finance/debt-management/interest-rate/ yield.html. The yield curve is fitted daily using a hermite cubic spline. For inputs, Treasury primarily uses the bid yields on the on-the-run securities (most recently auctioned Treasury securities in all maturity tranches that Treasury currently auctions) as of approximately 3:30 p.m. each trading day. CMT yields are based on semiannual interest payments and are read at constant maturity points to develop a consistent data series.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [138, 808, 798, 867], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"The quotations used by Treasury to calculate the bid yields and fit the yield curve are obtained by the Federal\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 271, 1492, 363], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"Reserve Bank of New York. The Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System also publishes the Treasury constant maturity data series in its weekly Statistical Release H.15.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [825, 365, 1499, 615], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"On July 31, 2001, Treasury expanded its constant maturity index to include a 1-month constant maturity yield, and Table MY-1 now includes a 1-month maturity beginning on that date. On February 18, 2002, Treasury discontinued the 30-year constant maturity yield. In lieu of the 30-year yield, Table MY-1 now includes a 20-year maturity. Historical data for the 20-year maturity is available from the Board of Governors' Statistical Release H.15.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [829, 618, 1488, 813], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"Prior to January 2003, this section also included data on long-term Treasury, corporate and municipal yields (Table MY-2). Effective January 2003, Table MY-2 and Chart MY-B were discontinued because Treasury no longer issues long-term bonds and no longer calculates or estimates long-term corporate rates.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [836, 816, 1486, 874], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"Chart MY-A, which previously was published in this section, has been discontinued.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [328, 900, 1293, 974], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"TABLE MY-1.\\u2014Treasury Market Bid Yields at Constant Maturities: Bills, Notes, and Bonds*\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 9, \"type\": \"caption\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [148, 990, 1466, 1886], \"page_id\": 54}], \"content\": \"<table><tr><th>Period</th><th>1-mo. (1)</th><th>3-mo. (2)</th><th>6-mo. (3)</th><th>1-yr. (4)</th><th>2-yr. (5)</th><th>3-yr. (6)</th><th>5-yr. (7)</th><th>7-yr. (8)</th><th>10-yr. (9)</th><th>20-yr. (10)</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\\\"11\\\">Monthly average:</td></tr><tr><td>2003 - July</td><td>0.90</td><td>0.92</td><td>0.97</td><td>1.12</td><td>1.47</td><td>1.93</td><td>2.87</td><td>3.45</td><td>3.98</td><td>4.92</td></tr><tr><td>Aug</td><td>0.95</td><td>0.97</td><td>1.05</td><td>1.31</td><td>1.86</td><td>2.44</td><td>3.37</td><td>3.96</td><td>4.45</td><td>5.39</td></tr><tr><td>Sept</td><td>0.91</td><td>0.96</td><td>1.03</td><td>1.24</td><td>1.71</td><td>2.23</td><td>3.18</td><td>3.74</td><td>4.27</td><td>5.21</td></tr><tr><td>Oct</td><td>0.91</td><td>0.94</td><td>1.02</td><td>1.25</td><td>1.75</td><td>2.26</td><td>3.19</td><td>3.75</td><td>4.29</td><td>5.21</td></tr><tr><td>Nov</td><td>0.94</td><td>0.95</td><td>1.04</td><td>1.34</td><td>1.93</td><td>2.45</td><td>3.29</td><td>3.81</td><td>4.30</td><td>5.17</td></tr><tr><td>Dec</td><td>0.89</td><td>0.91</td><td>1.01</td><td>1.31</td>