and liabilities payable in foreign currencies to foreign banks and to \\\"other foreigners.\\\"\\n6 Includes marketable U.S. Government bonds and notes held by foreign banks.\\n7 Principally the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development, the Inter-American Development Bank, and the Asian Development Bank.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [823, 1591, 1481, 1695], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"8 Data on the two lines shown for this date reflect different benchmark bases for foreigners' holdings of selected U.S. long-term securities. Figures on the first line are comparable to those for earlier dates; figures on the second line are based in part on benchmark surveys as of end-March 2000, end-June 2002, and end-June 2003, respectively, and are comparable to those shown for the following dates.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [818, 1702, 1481, 1832], \"page_id\": 58}], \"content\": \"Note.\\u2014Table is based on Treasury data and on data reported to the Treasury by banks, other depository institutions and brokers in the United States. Data generally correspond to statistics following in this section and in the \\\"Capital Movements\\\" section. Table excludes International Monetary Fund \\\"holdings of dollars\\\" and holdings of U.S. Treasury letters of credit and nonnegotiable noninterest-bearing special U.S. notes held by international and regional organizations.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 7, \"type\": \"footnote\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [550, 101, 1082, 120], \"page_id\": 59}], \"content\": \"INTERNATIONAL FINANCIAL STATISTICS\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1461, 101, 1486, 120], \"page_id\": 59}], \"content\": \"59\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [328, 200, 1310, 266], \"page_id\": 59}], \"content\": \"TABLE IFS-3.\\u201